@misc{sql-F1-carrier-unmodelled-is-not-residue,
  section  = {finding},
  claim    = {CARRIER-UNMODELLED is not RESIDUE, and collapsing them converts WORK into a WALL.},
  check    = {standing},
  note     = {kind=finding by=sql-oracle. Residue is a claim about the COMPUTATION — a Merkle fold or a log-sum-exp has no SQL aggregate, so it stays python. Carrier-unmodelled is a claim about what has been MODELLED: the walk is already a closure and lifts the moment its carrier has a relational form, WHICH NEED NOT BE DURABLE — a VALUES list, a CTE, an unnest, a temp table all serve. The generated census carries both counts separately for exactly this reason. STANDING. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): residue is a claim about the COMPUTATION; carrier-unmodelled is a claim about what has been MODELLED, and the carrier need not be durable}
}

