  check    = {standing},
  unification = {entailed},
  axis     = {010},
  note     = {kind=finding by=sql-oracle. ⚑ ENTAILED, two populated points. POINT ONE: a postgres temp-file spill is created, written and deleted INSIDE one statement, so pg_stat_activity structurally cannot observe it. POINT TWO: three samples of the correctly-chosen statement (INSERT INTO _ht_map) read clean while the durable log_temp_files jsonlog showed that exact statement spilling 577332 bytes. Two points force the third: the fix is a different KIND of instrument, not more samples. ⚑ THIS IS NOT a-sample-is-not-a-census — that framing suggests more samples would help, and they would not. Ask whether an instrument can see an event that starts and ends between two observations BEFORE reporting an absence from it. STANDING. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): a spill is created and deleted inside one statement, so no number of pg_stat_activity samples can observe it — a different KIND of instrument is needed}
}

