@misc{tmi-F5a-sppf-fanin-is-bimodal-not-discriminating,
  section  = {finding},
  claim    = {SPPF fan-in is bimodal — 58 percent of children are unshared and 0.017 percent absorb 27 percent of edges as AST boilerplate — so the sharing channel collapses content unless the head is cut},
  check    = {standing},
  note     = {kind=finding by=sppf-ingestion. Measured LIVE 2026-08-24 over node_child, corpus-wide — 440,604 distinct children, 1,733,430 parent edges, max fan-in 87,359. fan-in exactly 1 covers 256,644 children (58.2 percent). fan-in at or above 1000 covers 73 children (0.017 percent) absorbing 469,635 edges (27.1 percent), and q_fanin names them as syntactic scaffolding — Range' 87,359, Bool False 77,255, ArgInfo 70,387, Name 14,328, Fixity' 11,118, InScope 10,712. The discriminating band is the middle 183,887 children over 1,263,795 edges. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): tmi-F5's sharing-axis channel is priced, and it does NOT discriminate at the top. SPPF fan-in over node_child, LIVE 2026-08-24, corpus-wide: 440,604 distinct children carrying 1,733,430 parent edges, max fan-in 87,359. The distribution is BIMODAL, not heavy at low arity. Head: 256,644 of 440,604 children (58.2 percent) have fan-in exactly 1 — shared by nobody, so they carry no sharing signal at all. Tail: 73 children (0.017 percent) have fan-in >= 1000 and absorb 469,635 of 1,733,430 edges (27.1 percent). Those 73 are named by q_fanin and they are SYNTACTIC BOILERPLATE, not content — Range' at 87,359, Bool False at 77,255, ArgInfo at 70,387 and again 14,395, Name at 14,328, Fixity' at 11,118, InScope at 10,712, NoCatchall, NoEllipsis. The discriminating band is the MIDDLE: 183,960 children have fan-in >= 2, and stripping the >= 1000 tail leaves 183,887 sharing-bearing nodes over 1,263,795 edges. So read raw, the channel COLLAPSES DISTINCT CONTENT — 27 percent of its mass is Agda AST scaffolding every core contains. It becomes usable only with the boilerplate tail excluded, which means the apex-band statistic needs a head cut, not just a threshold.}
}

@misc{sql-F7-column-dependency-is-the-tree-not-the-plan,
