 p90 99,587, hi 4,592,031, max/median 471x. The tail by name: bbRKTCildS8 4,592,031 / 3rgG0rxNrU8 3,863,572 / VvIrBjiyKJ0 3,451,144 / Y537kmhoLJo 2,842,054 / mekIXTujyrM 2,769,429 / OPDN0KbHHGY 2,552,181 / qfL4hdKTgHs 1,217,543 / d41YwiedDD4 1,146,354. bbRKTCildS8 is the same 4.59M core the Ⓢ5 brief already sized with --height. The distribution is EXTREMELY heavy-tailed: median 9,753 against p90 99,587 and hi 4.59M, so the mean 48,720 sits at roughly the 80th percentile and is not a typical core. Consequence for Ⓢ5: the 7 largest units are 1.2M to 4.6M obs each while the median core is under 10k, so whatever bounds the peak has to be chosen for the tail and cannot be validated on a median core — --spread's own output says this, naming a median band for typical-case trials.}
