@misc{sql-F41-unit-freshness-taint-is-modelled-via-unit-obs,
  section  = {finding},
  claim    = {Per-row provenance for a core-derived name index joins _unit through unit_obs to core_fp, NOT _unit to core_fp directly -- file_id is an .agdai relpath and core_id is a content hash, so the direct join silently returns zero and reads as an absent capability.},
  check    = {standing},
  note     = {kind=finding by=sql-oracle. Witness: schema.py --probe on live. Direct join _unit JOIN terms ON term_id=file_id JOIN core_fp ON core_id=text -> 0 rows. Bridged join _unit JOIN unit_obs JOIN core_fp -> units_with_mtime=13800, cores=2688. Units with no unit_obs row: 1495 over 229 modules. core_fp.mtime is the CORE mtime (ns), not the source mtime, so fresh-vs-stale needs a source-mtime/digest column the store does not carry: CARRIER-UNMODELLED, not residue. ⚑ WITNESS NOTE, moved verbatim from findings.py WITNESSES (2026-09-26): PER-ROW FRESHNESS TAINT IS EXPRESSIBLE, but NOT by the join a reader first reaches for. _unit.file_id resolves through terms to an .agdai RELPATH (e.g. Algebra/F2/F2Cases.agdai), while core_fp.core_id is a CONTENT HASH (koYbaQr6TH0) -- so _unit JOIN core_fp ON core_id = file_id text returns ZERO rows and reads as 'the store cannot express freshness'. It can: unit_obs(core_id, unit_id) is the bridge. MEASURED live 2026-08-25: _unit JOIN unit_obs JOIN core_fp yields 13,800 of 15,295 units carrying an mtime, over 2,688 of 2,917 modules. The 1,495-unit / 229-module remainder has NO unit_obs row and is therefore provenance-less, a THIRD taint state distinct from fresh and stale. core_fp.mtime is the CORE's mtime in nanoseconds, not the SOURCE's, so the store alone cannot compute fresh-vs-stale -- that comparison needs a source stat, which is CARRIER-UNMODELLED (the carrier is a source-mtime or source-digest column), not residue.}
}

